The Python code snippet provided should help answer the question by utilizing the Text_Detector_Tool to detect Chinese characters in the image. Here's how you can use the Text_Detector_Tool command with the demonstration_path input, as per your requirements:

```python
from text_detector import Text_Detector_Tool

# Demonstration path
detection_image = "/path/to/detection/image.png"

# Language code for English, or 'Chinese'
language_code = "en"

# Depth estimation mode (True to estimate depth, False to skip)
depth_estimation_mode = True

# Output directory to save the depth images (if True, current directory)
outdir = './vis_depth'

result = Text_Detector_Tool.execute(image=detection_image, languages=[language_code], depth_estimation_mode=depth_estimation_mode)

# Export detection results
for result_dict in result:
    if result_dict["language"] == "en":
        for component in result_dict["results"]:
            if component["language"] == "en":
                print(f"Detected text: {component['text']}"), print(f"Confidence score: {component['confidence']}")
    if result_dict["language"] == "zh":
        for component in result_dict["results"]:
            if component["language"] == "zh":
                print(f"Detected Chinese characters: {component['to_translation']}"), print(f"Confidence score: {component['confidence']}")
```

Replace "/path/to/detection/image.png" with the actual path of the image file you want to detect Chinese characters in. This code will output the detected Chinese characters with their corresponding confidence scores and bounding box coordinates.
